---
// How I work: broad enough for any business, direct, no hedging.
---
<section id="how" class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head rv">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> How I work</p>
      <h2>From inside your business, one at a time.</h2>
      <p class="lead">I work from inside your organization. I see where the day gets stuck, build what is missing, and keep it running.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="hw">
      <ol class="hw-steps rv">
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>I start by looking at your daily workflow.</h3>
            <p>What a normal day looks like, what you interact with, and where the time goes: the things people re-type, re-check, or walk over to find out.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Then I build what is missing.</h3>
            <p>You see it early, and I iterate often as your team uses it, so it keeps fitting the way they actually work.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>It lives on top of what you already have.</h3>
            <p>Nothing is replaced, and your team stops wrestling with the old system. Your information stays inside your organization.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>I maintain it, and build the next piece when you want it.</h3>
            <p>I keep it running and check on it regularly, so I know when an issue comes up before you have to flag it.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="hw-side rv">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>A good fit</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>An owner or manager who wants hours back every day.</li>
            <li>A team ready for small changes that add up.</li>
            <li>A clinic, pharmacy, lab, farm or office where people are the glue between systems.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
